{
  "_createdAt": "2026-04-01T04:34:58Z",
  "_id": "703a284c-83bb-455c-9789-ef12074e15e4",
  "_rev": "pJuzvlAAkes31pzNsp7lKu",
  "_system": {
    "base": {
      "id": "703a284c-83bb-455c-9789-ef12074e15e4",
      "rev": "kMmNf3snj7GoQAhiUlidg0"
    }
  },
  "_type": "post",
  "_updatedAt": "2026-11-05T19:42:26Z",
  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "edit20261025-106",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-107",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "I added an ASUS Ascent GX10, based on NVIDIA GB10, to my lab to explore GPU workloads as infrastructure. It shares the GB10 platform with NVIDIA’s DGX Spark but is a distinct ASUS system. My field engineering work involved OpenStack, Kubernetes, and Ceph, so I wanted a node where several experiments could share the GPU."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "f6a25efb6178",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "f6a25efb60",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "This post covers how I set up MicroK8s alongside Docker, installed the NVIDIA GPU Operator, and configured GPU time-slicing so several workloads can share the GB10 GPU. Along the way, I’ll explain the MicroK8s-specific containerd paths that make this setup work."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "edit20261025-127",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-128",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Version and validation scope"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "edit20261025-129",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-130",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The commands retain MicroK8s "
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-131",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "1.32/stable"
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-132",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and GPU Operator "
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-133",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "v25.10.1"
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-134",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " from the original March 2026 notes. The host-driver version and original test date were not recorded. This October revision checks the documentation and image manifest; it does not retest the full stack or identify these pins as the latest supported combination."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "630f35e4b4e4",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "4a3679c18c52",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Installing MicroK8s"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "da31a8c326b5",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "sudo snap install microk8s --classic --channel=1.32/stable\nsudo microk8s status --wait-ready",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "fb8e2c6156b3",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "23398645c54b",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Add your user to the microk8s group:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "c1a115575944",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "sudo usermod -aG microk8s $USER\nnewgrp microk8s\nmicrok8s kubectl get nodes",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "eea8ce4d9071",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "eea8ce4d90",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Enable the core add-ons:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "620cd5daa7c7",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "microk8s enable dns\nmicrok8s enable hostpath-storage\nmicrok8s enable helm3",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "11d386822d7c",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "11d3868220",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Create aliases for "
        },
        {
          "_key": "11d3868221",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "kubectl"
        },
        {
          "_key": "11d3868222",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "11d3868223",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "helm"
        },
        {
          "_key": "11d3868224",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " so you do not have to prefix every command with "
        },
        {
          "_key": "11d3868225",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "microk8s"
        },
        {
          "_key": "11d3868226",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ":"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "347b629c3c63",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "echo \"alias kubectl='microk8s kubectl'\" >> ~/.bashrc\necho \"alias helm='microk8s helm3'\" >> ~/.bashrc\nsource ~/.bashrc",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "3bf6efcf6c41",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "3bf6efcf60",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Docker and MicroK8s Use Separate Image Stores"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "65e5fbe3c82c",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "65e5fbe3c0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Docker and MicroK8s use separate container runtimes, so an image pulled with "
        },
        {
          "_key": "65e5fbe3c1",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "docker pull"
        },
        {
          "_key": "65e5fbe3c2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " is not automatically available to a Kubernetes pod, and vice versa. To use a locally built Docker image in MicroK8s, import it:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "253cf8a30d5b",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "docker tag myimage:latest myimage:local\ndocker save myimage:local | microk8s ctr images import -",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "f28cac962a0a",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "f28cac9620",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "In the pod specification, use "
        },
        {
          "_key": "f28cac9621",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "image: myimage:local"
        },
        {
          "_key": "f28cac9622",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "f28cac9623",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "imagePullPolicy: Never"
        },
        {
          "_key": "f28cac9624",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " to run the imported image without contacting a registry. The image must support the GX10’s Arm architecture. On a multi-node cluster, import it on every node where the pod could run, or publish it to a registry instead. Docker and MicroK8s can each pull registry-hosted images independently."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "a0d3eb5580ce",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "089e390d882c",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Installing the NVIDIA GPU Operator"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "edit20261025-108",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-109",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The GPU Operator manages the components that expose NVIDIA GPUs to Kubernetes workloads. In this setup the host’s NVIDIA driver is already installed and managed outside Kubernetes, so I disable the operator’s driver component and let it configure the runtime and device plugin."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "5a74b7200983",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "9310044bfce7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Add the NVIDIA Helm Repository"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "c3a0e9fa2696",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "helm repo add nvidia https://helm.ngc.nvidia.com/nvidia\nhelm repo update nvidia\nhelm repo list | grep nvidia",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "ee59e87c9c50",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "949a0035dc44",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Install the GPU Operator"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "edit20261025-110",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-111",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The key flag is "
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-112",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "--set driver.enabled=false"
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-113",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". The host already has a driver, so I leave that component disabled. The operator still manages the container toolkit and the other enabled components. Verify this assumption on your own host before using the command."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "59f1085e21b0",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "59f1085e20",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Because MicroK8s is packaged as a snap, its containerd socket and configuration files live under "
        },
        {
          "_key": "59f1085e21",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "/var/snap/microk8s/"
        },
        {
          "_key": "59f1085e22",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " rather than the usual system paths. The GPU Operator needs those exact locations, so I pass three environment variables explicitly:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "b7d730a3b466",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "helm install gpu-operator -n gpu-operator --create-namespace \\\n  nvidia/gpu-operator \\\n  --version=v25.10.1 \\\n  --set driver.enabled=false \\\n  --set toolkit.enabled=true \\\n  --set toolkit.env[0].name=CONTAINERD_CONFIG \\\n  --set toolkit.env[0].value=/var/snap/microk8s/current/args/containerd-template.toml \\\n  --set toolkit.env[1].name=CONTAINERD_SOCKET \\\n  --set toolkit.env[1].value=/var/snap/microk8s/common/run/containerd.sock \\\n  --set toolkit.env[2].name=RUNTIME_CONFIG_SOURCE \\\n  --set-string toolkit.env[2].value=file=/var/snap/microk8s/current/args/containerd.toml",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "211508f5d3cf",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "211508f5d0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "These paths are a common failure point when deploying the GPU Operator on snap-based Kubernetes. If the operator cannot reach containerd, its pods may enter "
        },
        {
          "_key": "211508f5d1",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "CrashLoopBackOff"
        },
        {
          "_key": "211508f5d2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " with a socket error. Canonical Kubernetes uses different containerd locations that depend on its configured base directory, so verify the actual socket and configuration paths before adapting this command."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "bfa9717966a0",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "bfa9717960",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Verify GPU Access"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "edit20261025-114",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-115",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Create a test pod using NVIDIA’s CUDA vector-add sample. As of October 25, 2026, this tag’s registry manifest contains both "
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-116",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "linux/arm64"
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-117",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-118",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "linux/amd64"
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-119",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " images. That confirms architecture availability, not a fresh execution test on GB10; check the pod events and logs on the actual host."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "d94e33ce01a0",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "# cuda-test.yaml\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: cuda-vectoradd\nspec:\n  restartPolicy: OnFailure\n  runtimeClassName: nvidia\n  containers:\n  - name: cuda-vectoradd\n    image: \"nvcr.io/nvidia/k8s/cuda-sample:vectoradd-cuda12.5.0-ubuntu22.04\"\n    resources:\n      limits:\n        nvidia.com/gpu: 1",
      "language": "yaml"
    },
    {
      "_key": "5470281057f2",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "kubectl apply -f cuda-test.yaml\nkubectl logs cuda-vectoradd",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "edit20261025-120",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-121",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "NVIDIA’s documented successful sample output looks like this; it is an example, not a new test log from this revision:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "b3ae47797c9f",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "[Vector addition of 50000 elements]\nCopy input data from the host memory to the CUDA device\nCUDA kernel launch with 196 blocks of 256 threads\nCopy output data from the CUDA device to the host memory\nTest PASSED\nDone",
      "language": "text"
    },
    {
      "_key": "1f5925b193cb",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "# Clean up\nkubectl delete -f cuda-test.yaml",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "f7aa84a297a0",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "aa8220e4cddd",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "GPU Time-Slicing: Running Multiple Workloads on One GPU"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "bea659bd7c39",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "bea659bd70",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "By default, Kubernetes advertises each GPU as an indivisible resource, so a node with one GPU can satisfy only one request for "
        },
        {
          "_key": "bea659bd71",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "nvidia.com/gpu: 1"
        },
        {
          "_key": "bea659bd72",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " at a time. That default can be restrictive on the GX10, which has 128 GB of coherent unified system memory. Workloads such as Jupyter notebooks, inference services, and training jobs can often coexist."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "21b17138b423",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "21b17138b0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "GPU time-slicing lets the NVIDIA device plugin advertise one physical GPU as several allocatable replicas and interleave workloads that share it. Unlike MIG, time-slicing provides no memory or fault isolation between replicas, so workloads share the same unified memory budget. Plan capacity accordingly."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "c0a85369cba3",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "6d7c4097aa32",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Step 1: Create the Time-Slicing ConfigMap"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "c403692a28fc",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "cat <<'EOF' | kubectl apply -n gpu-operator -f -\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  name: time-slicing-config\ndata:\n  any: |-\n    version: v1\n    flags:\n      migStrategy: none\n    sharing:\n      timeSlicing:\n        resources:\n        - name: nvidia.com/gpu\n          replicas: 4\nEOF",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "edit20261025-122",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-123",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "replicas: 4"
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-124",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " advertises four scheduling slots backed by the same physical GPU. It does not create four GPUs, reserve four equal memory partitions, or guarantee four workloads will fit."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "038f0dfa712b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "43dde39294f2",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Step 2: Patch the ClusterPolicy"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "c699bd7f6143",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "kubectl patch clusterpolicy/cluster-policy -n gpu-operator --type merge -p \\\n  '{\"spec\":{\"devicePlugin\":{\"config\":{\"name\":\"time-slicing-config\",\"default\":\"any\"}}}}'",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "e6e72e400c96",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "1c9f15b8d0b7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Step 3: Restart the Device Plugin"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "e7a8ef138df3",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "kubectl delete pod -n gpu-operator -l app=nvidia-device-plugin-daemonset",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "db9e3c585e48",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "203e5dd1e2cf",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Step 4: Verify"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "b6275fa75a6b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "1f307e2131e6",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Wait 30–60 seconds, then:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "e76008189eb8",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "kubectl describe node | grep nvidia.com/gpu",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "a2c70b0717d7",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b545b2f840c4",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Expected output:"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "85fe78ee1b5c",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "nvidia.com/gpu.replicas=4\nnvidia.com/gpu.sharing-strategy=time-slicing\nnvidia.com/gpu.product=NVIDIA-GB10-SHARED\nnvidia.com/gpu:     4\nnvidia.com/gpu:     4",
      "language": "text"
    },
    {
      "_key": "6ae53fae4a3b",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "6ae53fae40",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The "
        },
        {
          "_key": "6ae53fae41",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "-SHARED"
        },
        {
          "_key": "6ae53fae42",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " product suffix, "
        },
        {
          "_key": "6ae53fae43",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "nvidia.com/gpu.replicas=4"
        },
        {
          "_key": "6ae53fae44",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " label, and "
        },
        {
          "_key": "6ae53fae45",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "sharing-strategy=time-slicing"
        },
        {
          "_key": "6ae53fae46",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " label confirm that time-slicing is active. Each pod still requests "
        },
        {
          "_key": "6ae53fae47",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ],
          "text": "nvidia.com/gpu: 1"
        },
        {
          "_key": "6ae53fae48",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "; the NVIDIA device plugin manages shared access to the physical GPU."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "d4f3f0854720",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "7f0e888d38f8",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Adjusting or Disabling Time-Slicing"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "2a27b4ee7362",
      "_type": "code",
      "code": "# Change the replica count\nkubectl edit configmap time-slicing-config -n gpu-operator\nkubectl delete pod -n gpu-operator -l app=nvidia-device-plugin-daemonset\n\n# Revert to exclusive access\nkubectl patch clusterpolicy/cluster-policy -n gpu-operator --type merge -p \\\n  '{\"spec\":{\"devicePlugin\":{\"config\":{\"name\":\"\",\"default\":\"\"}}}}'\nkubectl delete configmap time-slicing-config -n gpu-operator\nkubectl delete pod -n gpu-operator -l app=nvidia-device-plugin-daemonset",
      "language": "bash"
    },
    {
      "_key": "edit20261025-125",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-126",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "With this setup, the GX10 can host several GPU experiments through MicroK8s. The GPU Operator handles integration, while time-slicing shares execution on one GPU without memory or fault isolation."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "edit20261025-135",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-136",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Memory pressure still belongs to the host"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "edit20261025-137",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-138",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Time-sliced workloads share the GB10 memory pool. My "
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-140",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "edit20261025-139"
          ],
          "text": "memory-pressure investigation"
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-141",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " explains why a model load can also affect SSH and other host services. Its guard scans Docker cgroups; it does not monitor or stop MicroK8s/containerd pods. Do not treat it as protection for this Kubernetes setup."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-139",
          "_type": "contentLink",
          "href": "https://adithya-rajendran.com/blog/dgx-spark-unified-memory-oom-hardening"
        }
      ],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "edit20261025-142",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-143",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "References: "
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-145",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "edit20261025-144"
          ],
          "text": "NVIDIA GPU Operator validation example"
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-146",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and the "
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-148",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "edit20261025-147"
          ],
          "text": "CUDA sample image catalog"
        },
        {
          "_key": "edit20261025-149",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". The image tag checked here is "
        },
        {
